{
  "description": "What an analysis is doing right now, including the coarse tier that used to be invisible from outside the process.",
  "editable": true,
  "links": [
    {
      "asDropdown": false,
      "icon": "external link",
      "includeVars": false,
      "keepTime": true,
      "tags": [],
      "targetBlank": true,
      "title": "Find the trace for one file",
      "tooltip": "Per-FILE and per-CHUNK detail lives only in traces -- metrics carry no file dimension by construction.",
      "type": "link",
      "url": "/explore?left={\"datasource\":\"${tracesource}\",\"queries\":[{\"query\":\"{ resource.service.name = \"phaze-analysis\" }\"}]}"
    }
  ],
  "panels": [
    {
      "collapsed": false,
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 1,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0
      },
      "id": 1,
      "panels": [],
      "title": "Right now",
      "type": "row"
    },
    {
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "description": "The signal that did not exist before this epic. The UI progress channel is fine-tier-only by design, so a running analysis reported nothing at all for the coarse tier -- 94.69% of wall clock on the 4,761.835 s file phaze-zaf2l measured. That share is DURATION-DEPENDENT: on a 10 h 03 m file the coarse tier is 50.7% and the fine tier 49.3% (phaze-bg115). The blind spot is the same either way; only its size moves.",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "custom": {
            "fillOpacity": 8,
            "lineWidth": 2,
            "showPoints": "never"
          },
          "unit": "/min"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 1
      },
      "id": 2,
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "calcs": [
            "mean",
            "max"
          ],
          "displayMode": "table",
          "placement": "bottom"
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "sum by (tier) (rate(phaze_analysis_windows_total{job=~\"$job\", outcome=\"analyzed\"}[$__rate_interval])) * 60",
          "instant": false,
          "legendFormat": "{{tier}}",
          "range": true,
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "title": "Windows completed / min",
      "type": "timeseries"
    },
    {
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "description": "One sweep is one of the 34 graphs run across every buffer of one chunk. The coarse tier can go many minutes without completing a WINDOW while completing sweeps steadily -- this is the finer liveness read.",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "custom": {
            "fillOpacity": 8,
            "lineWidth": 2,
            "showPoints": "never"
          },
          "unit": "/min"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 1
      },
      "id": 3,
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "calcs": [
            "mean",
            "max"
          ],
          "displayMode": "table",
          "placement": "bottom"
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "sum(rate(phaze_analysis_model_sweep_duration_seconds_count{job=~\"$job\"}[$__rate_interval])) * 60",
          "instant": false,
          "legendFormat": "sweeps",
          "range": true,
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "title": "Model sweeps completed / min",
      "type": "timeseries"
    },
    {
      "collapsed": false,
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 1,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 9
      },
      "id": 4,
      "panels": [],
      "title": "Coverage and failures",
      "type": "row"
    },
    {
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "description": "A skip is a window dropped rather than a file failed -- a decode that produced no audio, a model that killed the window, a derivation that raised. Steady non-zero here is coverage quietly eroding.",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "custom": {
            "fillOpacity": 8,
            "lineWidth": 2,
            "showPoints": "never"
          },
          "unit": "/min"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 10
      },
      "id": 5,
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "calcs": [
            "mean",
            "max"
          ],
          "displayMode": "table",
          "placement": "bottom"
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "sum by (tier) (rate(phaze_analysis_windows_total{job=~\"$job\", outcome=\"skipped\"}[$__rate_interval])) * 60",
          "instant": false,
          "legendFormat": "{{tier}}",
          "range": true,
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "title": "Windows skipped / min (per-window failure isolation firing)",
      "type": "timeseries"
    },
    {
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "description": "",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "custom": {
            "fillOpacity": 60,
            "lineWidth": 1,
            "showPoints": "never",
            "stacking": {
              "group": "A",
              "mode": "normal"
            }
          },
          "unit": "/h"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 10
      },
      "id": 6,
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "calcs": [
            "mean",
            "max"
          ],
          "displayMode": "table",
          "placement": "bottom"
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "sum by (outcome) (rate(phaze_analysis_run_duration_seconds_count{job=~\"$job\"}[$__rate_interval])) * 3600",
          "instant": false,
          "legendFormat": "{{outcome}}",
          "range": true,
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "title": "Analysis outcomes / hour",
      "type": "timeseries"
    },
    {
      "collapsed": false,
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 1,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 18
      },
      "id": 7,
      "panels": [],
      "title": "Memory -- the D-07 / D-09 invariant, made watchable",
      "type": "row"
    },
    {
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "description": "A FLAT line is the invariant holding. A line with SLOPE is duration-linear growth, which is a BUG and never a sizing input -- phaze-b2qs9 measured +0.31 GiB per fine chunk before the D-09 fix, reaching 10.28 GiB at 12 h against a 4 GiB pod limit. Do not raise a limit to flatten this panel.",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "custom": {
            "fillOpacity": 8,
            "lineWidth": 2,
            "showPoints": "never"
          },
          "unit": "bytes"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 16,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 19
      },
      "id": 8,
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "calcs": [
            "mean",
            "max"
          ],
          "displayMode": "table",
          "placement": "bottom"
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.99, sum(rate(phaze_analysis_chunk_peak_rss_bytes_bucket{job=~\"$job\"}[$__rate_interval])) by (le, tier))",
          "instant": false,
          "legendFormat": "p99 {{tier}}",
          "range": true,
          "refId": "A"
        },
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "sum(rate(phaze_analysis_chunk_peak_rss_bytes_sum{job=~\"$job\"}[$__rate_interval])) by (tier) / sum(rate(phaze_analysis_chunk_peak_rss_bytes_count{job=~\"$job\"}[$__rate_interval])) by (tier)",
          "instant": false,
          "legendFormat": "mean {{tier}}",
          "range": true,
          "refId": "B"
        }
      ],
      "title": "Peak RSS at chunk boundaries",
      "type": "timeseries"
    },
    {
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "description": "",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "custom": {
            "fillOpacity": 8,
            "lineWidth": 2,
            "showPoints": "never"
          },
          "unit": "/min"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 8,
        "x": 16,
        "y": 19
      },
      "id": 9,
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "calcs": [
            "mean",
            "max"
          ],
          "displayMode": "table",
          "placement": "bottom"
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "sum by (tier) (rate(phaze_analysis_chunks_total{job=~\"$job\"}[$__rate_interval])) * 60",
          "instant": false,
          "legendFormat": "{{tier}}",
          "range": true,
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "title": "Chunks completed / min",
      "type": "timeseries"
    }
  ],
  "refresh": "30s",
